 "reportTemplate": {
  "summary": "Auto-refresh interval set to 1m and dashboard saved explicitly. Continuing from the partially-replayed procedure s_9969ed (its first 3 steps had already run, leaving a Share drawer open, which I closed), the top-bar refresh control showed \"1m\". No Save dashboard button exists in view mode, so I clicked Edit (toolbar then had Add/Settings/Exit edit/Save dashboard/More save options) and clicked Save dashboard. The save dialog opened with the 'Update default refresh value — Will make the current refresh the new default' checkbox unticked and Save disabled (\"No changes to save\"); I ticked the checkbox (dialog showed Changes1 and Save became enabled) and clicked Save — the app displayed the \"Dashboard saved\" alert. A clean reload of the dashboard URL with no refresh parameter still renders the top-bar refresh dropdown as \"1m\" (aria \"Choose refresh time interval with current interval 1 minute selected\"), proving the refresh interval persisted; the time range still reads \"Last 6 hours\" and both panels are present.",
  "values": {
   "main_button": "Last 6 hours",
   "ref": "s_9969ed"
  }
 },
